== Bugs ==
{{Bug|Resuming a {{C|Jacob and Esau}} run with Found Soul equipped in Esau's trinket slot will require a controller to continue. If a controller is available and plugged in, Found Soul can be controlled like a [[Co-op]] baby and won't mimic either brother's movements. This effect won't happen if Jacob holds the trinket. If no controller is available, the run is softlocked and cannot be continued.}}
{{Bug|When used together with {{T|Azazel's Stump}}, the soul familiar sometimes keeps {{C|Azazel}}'s properties (flight and short brimstone) for a few rooms after Isaac has transformed back to normal. {{T|Lil Clot}} also has this bug.}}
{{bug|If {{i|Sulfur}} has been used in a room before picking up Found Soul, it will retain Brimstone until dropped/killed, even through rooms.}}
{{bug|Entering one of the portals created by {{I|Card Reading}}, {{I|Lil Portal}}, and {{I|Ventricle Razor}} causes the familiar to become invisible until Isaac drops and picks up the trinket again. Entering a new floor sometimes also causes this bug.}}
{{bug|It is possible for both Isaac and the soul to target the same enemy/boss with {{i|Suplex!}} (easier to do on enemies with large hitboxes such as {{e|Hush}}). In this case, the enemy/boss may become invulnerable and/or invisible after the slam. Dropping the trinket or having the soul die does not fix the situation.}}
{{bug|If Isaac's items are rerolled (via {{i|D4}} or similar effects) while Found Soul is held, the soul will look like Isaac's detached head or his headless body. Dropping the trinket and picking it up again returns the soul its normal appearance.}}

